319 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 230 0 R
/E (Technology for Divyangjan, Kanpur, I spent the six weeks of this internship designing, training, testing and deploying AgriVision, a computer-vision application that detects crops and weeds in field images. The work covered the full machine-learning life cycle: understanding the problem, studying the data, fine- tuning a YOLO11n object detection model, building a Streamlit dashboard around it, evaluating the results and publishing the app online.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
320 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 230 0 R
/E (A relevant internship is important for career development because classroom learning rarely shows how much work lies between a working model and a usable product. Working on a real problem taught me to deal with practical limits such as image quality, model errors, deployment constraints and clear communication of results, which are the skills industry expects from a fresh engineer.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
321 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 230 0 R
/E (My project addresses weed detection in agriculture. Weeds compete with crops for water, light and nutrients, and finding them by walking through a field is slow and subjective. AgriVision lets a user upload a photo of a field, runs a trained object detector, draws a box around every crop plant and weed it finds, reports confidence scores and counts, and offers general crop-protection guidance.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
322 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 230 0 R
/E (This opportunity was provided by upskill Campus and The IoT Academy in association with UniConverge Technologies Pvt Ltd \(UCT\). It gave me a structured way to work on an industrial-style problem statement with a fixed timeline, a working deliverable and a final report.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
