475 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 236 0 R
/E (Weeds compete with crops for sunlight, water and nutrients and, if they are not controlled in time, reduce yield and quality. On most farms weed monitoring is still done by walking through the field and judging by eye, which is slow, tiring, inconsistent between people and hard to do over large areas. Spraying the whole field with herbicide is a common response, but it wastes chemicals, raises cost and harms the environment.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
476 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 236 0 R
/E (The problem I worked on was therefore: given a photograph of a field, automatically locate each crop plant and weed with a bounding box and a confidence score, summarise the result in a form a farmer or agronomist can understand, and show general crop-protection guidance, all through a simple web interface that needs no technical knowledge. The solution had to:)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
