/T (This image had no ground-truth labels, so this is a qualitative observation, not a measured error. Both boxes are large and overlap heavily over a dense leafy canopy, and no crop was reported although the image appears to show mostly crop plants. This suggests that dense, close-up or oblique images are harder for the model, and that a result should be checked against the image before acting on it. Interface and guidance \(T3 to T5\). The sliders, both themes \(Figures 3 and 4\) and the Crop Protection page \(Figure 6\) worked as expected; slider sweeps were not recorded.)
/E (This image had no ground-truth labels, so this is a qualitative observation, not a measured error. Both boxes are large and overlap heavily over a dense leafy canopy, and no crop was reported although the image appears to show mostly crop plants. This suggests that dense, close-up or oblique images are harder for the model, and that a result should be checked against the image before acting on it. Interface and guidance \(T3 to T5\). The sliders, both themes \(Figures 3 and 4\) and the Crop Protection page \(Figure 6\) worked as expected; slider sweeps were not recorded.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [29]
>>
